<title>NEW ZEALAND: CRICKET-NZ-SRI LANKA 4TH DAY SCOREBOARD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NZ-SRI LANKA 4TH DAY SCOREBOARD.</headline>
<dateline>DUNEDIN, New Zealand 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scoreboard on the</p>
<p>fourth day of the first cricket test between New Zealand and Sri</p>
<p>Lanka on Monday:</p>
<p>New Zealand first innings 586 for seven declared</p>
<p>Sri Lanka first innings 222</p>
<p>Sri Lanka second innings (37 without loss overnight)</p>
<p> S. Jayasuriya c Parore b Doull	     50</p>
<p> R. Mahanama b Doull			    21</p>
<p> M. Atapattu b Patel			    22</p>
<p> A. de Silva lbw b Astle			 0</p>
<p> A. Ranatunga c Horne b Vettori	     13</p>
<p> H. Tillekaratne run out			 8 </p>
<p> R. Kaluwitharana c and b Vettori	  103</p>
<p> C. Vaas c and b Davis			  57</p>
<p> P. Wickremasinghe c Doull b Astle	   0</p>
<p> N. Zoysa not out				 16</p>
<p> M. Muralitharan c and b Doull		26</p>
<p> Extras (lb-9 nb-3)			     12</p>
<p> Total (86.3 overs)			    328</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-49 2-82 3-85 4-99 5-115 6-133 7-270 8-271</p>
<p>9-285</p>
<p>Bowling: Doull 20.3-5-82-3, Davis 22-2-79-1 (nb-2), Horne</p>
<p>4-2-18-0, Astle 15-3-51-2 (nb-1), Patel 10-3-36-1, Vettori</p>
<p>15-3-53-2.</p>
<p>Result: New Zealand win by an innings and 36 runs. New</p>
<p>Zealand lead two-match series 1-0.</p>
